    <briefdescription>
<para><ref refid="classllvm_1_1_value" kindref="compound">Value</ref> handle that tracks a <ref refid="classllvm_1_1_value" kindref="compound">Value</ref> across RAUW. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><ref refid="classllvm_1_1_tracking_v_h" kindref="compound">TrackingVH</ref> is designed for situations where a client needs to hold a handle to a <ref refid="classllvm_1_1_value" kindref="compound">Value</ref> (or subclass) across some operations which may move that value, but should never destroy it or replace it with some unacceptable type.</para>
<para>It is an error to attempt to replace a value with one of a type which is incompatible with any of its outstanding TrackingVHs.</para>
<para>It is an error to read from a <ref refid="classllvm_1_1_tracking_v_h" kindref="compound">TrackingVH</ref> that does not point to a valid value. A <ref refid="classllvm_1_1_tracking_v_h" kindref="compound">TrackingVH</ref> is said to not point to a valid value if either it hasn&apos;t yet been assigned a value yet or because the value it was tracking has since been deleted.</para>
<para>Assigning a value to a <ref refid="classllvm_1_1_tracking_v_h" kindref="compound">TrackingVH</ref> is always allowed, even if said <ref refid="classllvm_1_1_tracking_v_h" kindref="compound">TrackingVH</ref> no longer points to a valid value. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
